  "question": {
    "text": "If the minimum area of the triangle formed by a tangent to the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and the co-ordinate axis is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is equal to ___________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0058_58ccc3c7b600.png\" style=\"width: 255px; height: 229px;\" /></p><p>Equation of tangent at parametric point&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to the ellipse is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Co-ordinates of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p>Therefore, Area&nbsp;of triangle formed by tangent and co-ordinate axes<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;therefore we can say Minimum area of triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
